{"content":[{"c":["CAPHTOR*, CAPHTORIM*, CAPHTORITES"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Place-name and the name of the people associated with the place. The Caphtorim among the Hamitic peoples in the “table of nations” are listed as the “sons” of Egypt (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.10.13-14","r":"Gen.10.13-14","rawR":"Gen.10.13-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.10.13-14","value":"Gen.10.13-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 10:13-14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.12","r":"1Chr.1.12","rawR":"1Chr.1.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.12","value":"1Chr.1.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 1:12"},", ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," “Caphthorim”). The text makes the Casluhim the parent people of the Philistines. However, prophets referred to the Philistines as colonists from Caphtor (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.47.4","r":"Jer.47.4","rawR":"Jer.47.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.47.4","value":"Jer.47.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 47:4"},"; see ",{"href":"?bref=Amos.9.7","r":"Amos.9.7","rawR":"Amos.9.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Amos.9.7","value":"Amos.9.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Am 9:7"},"). This has been the basis for some translators to transpose the clause of ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.10.14","r":"Gen.10.14","rawR":"Gen.10.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.10.14","value":"Gen.10.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Genesis 10:14"}," and to translate “Caphtorites, from whom the Philistines were descended” (",{"c":["neb"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). Others understand that although the Philistines may originally have been a Casluhian colony, they settled in regions that became known primarily as those of the Caphtorites."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Caphtor is referred to as ",{"c":["Kaptara"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," in Accadian, ",{"c":["kptr"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," in Ugaritic, and ",{"c":["Keftiu"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," in Egyptian. These references are to be dated from as early as 2200 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," down to about 1200 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},". The Egyptian sources are especially helpful in identifying Caphtor as Crete. On the other hand, there is a Jewish tradition that the Caphtorim were from Cappadocia; the Septuagint reads “Cappadocia” instead of “Caphtor.” This has led some to suggest that Caphtor is to be identified with a coastal region of Asia Minor or with the island of Carpathos. Perhaps by the 13th century ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},", “Caphtor” was used in a broad sense for the Aegean area from which the Philistines came."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["The Caphtorim are mentioned also as a people who invaded the region around Gaza, dispossessed the Avvim, and settled there (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.2.23","r":"Deut.2.23","rawR":"Deut.2.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.2.23","value":"Deut.2.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 2:23"},"). It appears that the Caphtorim were firmly settled around Gaza before Israel crossed the Jordan at the time of the Conquest. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=CasluhimCasluhites_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"CasluhimCasluhites_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"CasluhimCasluhites_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Casluhim, Casluhites"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"CaphtorCaphtorimCaphtorites","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 10:13-14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.10.13-14","rawQueryValue":"Gen.10.13-14","sourceRefExact":"Gen.10.13-14"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 1:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.1.12","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.1.12","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.1.12"},{"anchorText":"Jer 47:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.47.4","rawQueryValue":"Jer.47.4","sourceRefExact":"Jer.47.4"},{"anchorText":"Am 9:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Amos.9.7","rawQueryValue":"Amos.9.7","sourceRefExact":"Amos.9.7"},{"anchorText":"Genesis 10:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.10.14","rawQueryValue":"Gen.10.14","sourceRefExact":"Gen.10.14"},{"anchorText":"Dt 2:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.2.23","rawQueryValue":"Deut.2.23","sourceRefExact":"Deut.2.23"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"9ba00f624219be8fb1b13446f3058a930a55b72799d9fd2b7d0a694986252441","sourceItemName":"CaphtorCaphtorimCaphtorites","sourceItemOrder":45,"sourceMember":"Articles/C.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[{"name":"AerialViewOfAncientSynagogueInCapernaum","src":"../Pictures/Pictures.xml"}]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"CaphtorCaphtorimCaphtorites","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Caphtor*, Caphtorim*, Caphtorites","title":"Caphtor*, Caphtorim*, Caphtorites","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}